/data on a partition of its own when the phone has one, else the 4 GB RAM disk as before:
- mount-data.sh (vendor/etc): init runs it with syncexec (exec does not wait) at the start of the vendor pre-init
  job, where 0001 mounted the tmpfs. It looks for the GPT partition named "ohdata" (scripts/14-data-partition.sh
  makes one from the end of Android's userdata), makes its device node if ueventd has not yet, runs e2fsck -p
  (e2fsck -y when that leaves errors: a hard reset is common on this phone and nobody is there to answer) and
  mounts it ext4 on /data. Without the partition, or when it does not mount, /data is the tmpfs of 0001.
- the token setup after the mount stays as 0001 has it (the system init.cfg runs it on the read-only root first)

